 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "In 1969, Sergei Stepanov found an elementary way to prove such bounds,",
   "start": 0.75,
   "end": 6.0
  },
  {
   "text": "later extended to all curves by Bombieri and Schmidt.",
   "start": 6.0,
   "end": 9.65
  },
  {
   "text": "Its engine is simple.",
   "start": 9.65,
   "end": 11.487
  },
  {
   "text": "A polynomial of degree D has at most D roots, counted with multiplicity:",
   "start": 11.487,
   "end": 16.312
  },
  {
   "text": "a double root counts twice.",
   "start": 16.312,
   "end": 18.35
  },
  {
   "text": "So build an auxiliary polynomial that vanishes at every one of the N solutions,",
   "start": 19.275,
   "end": 23.962
  },
  {
   "text": "each to order m.",
   "start": 23.962,
   "end": 24.925
  },
  {
   "text": "Counting roots gives N times m, at most D.",
   "start": 24.925,
   "end": 27.738
  },
  {
   "text": "Push m up while keeping D in check,",
   "start": 27.738,
   "end": 29.975
  },
  {
   "text": "and the competing error terms balance when m is about root p.",
   "start": 29.975,
   "end": 33.4
  },
  {
   "text": "That's the moral: multiplicity of about root p is what yields an error of about root",
   "start": 33.4,
   "end": 38.8
  },
  {
   "text": "p.",
   "start": 38.8,
   "end": 39.25
  }
 ],
